  "question": {
    "text": "In the shown wireframe, each side of a square (the smallest square) has a resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math>. What is the equivalent resistance value (in ohm) of the circuit between the points <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0118_e8cfa5530cee.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 142px; width: 250px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "14",
  "solution": {
    "text": "The circuit can be folded about <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and redrawn as<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0118_98f1c55e2fa3.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 359px; height: 203px;\" /><br /><br />Hence equivalent resistance between <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>."
  }
